{
  "id": "task_002",
  "title": "LRU Cache with TTL Expiry",
  "language": "python",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "source": "Custom \u2014 LRU + TTL combined",
  "description": "Implement a class `LRUCache` with time-to-live (TTL) expiry.\n\n`__init__(self, capacity: int)` \u2014 sets max capacity.\n\n`get(self, key: int, now: int) -> int` \u2014 returns the value if the key exists AND has not expired (i.e. `inserted_at + ttl > now`). Returns -1 otherwise. A successful get counts as a use (updates LRU order).\n\n`put(self, key: int, value: int, ttl: int, now: int) -> None` \u2014 inserts or updates the key with the given value and TTL. If the key already exists, update its value and reset its TTL. When at capacity, first lazily evict any expired keys; if still at capacity, evict the Least Recently Used key.\n\nIf `capacity == 0`, the cache stores nothing.\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int): ...\n    def get(self, key: int, now: int) -> int: ...\n    def put(self, key: int, value: int, ttl: int, now: int) -> None: ...",
  "function_signature": "class LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int): ...\n    def get(self, key: int, now: int) -> int: ...\n    def put(self, key: int, value: int, ttl: int, now: int) -> None: ...",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= capacity <= 3000",
    "0 <= key <= 10^4",
    "0 <= value <= 10^5",
    "1 <= ttl <= 10^6",
    "0 <= now <= 10^9",
    "now is non-decreasing across operations"
  ],
